  "limitations": [
    "Three repetitions per workload/concurrency in one sequential stable-then-candidate session; no confidence interval, randomized crossover or long-duration tail-latency claim.",
    "The only worse median TTFT is C2/16K: 327.0 ms stable versus 505.8 ms candidate (+178.8 ms); observed ranges overlap, and median request duration improves from 19.126 s to 10.297 s.",
    "Short C1 reasoning baseline includes one slow observation (41.27 tok/s versus median 52.19); aggregate short C1 improvement is influenced by that observation, while all candidate observations still exceed the baseline maximum.",
    "Output trajectories can differ across profiles and concurrent repetitions. Identical greedy outputs are not a universal guarantee; expected-result correctness gates remain separate.",
    "Context measurements are warm RAM-prefix workloads after harness warmups; they do not measure cold 4K/16K prefill performance.",
    "The comparison includes runner, drafter, upstream/source changes, memory utilization and fairness settings; it cannot attribute the gain to DFlash2 alone.",
    "Per-position acceptance counters are phase-wide, not per workload. SSE event gaps are not individual-token latency under speculation.",
    "This artifact does not by itself qualify 262K execution, all vision/tools/cancellation cases, production frontend behavior or higher sustained concurrency; retain the separate exact-package qualification gates.",
    "The user-reported 10\u201315 s delay after roughly a day idle remains unreproduced; these warmed performance measurements do not resolve it."
